# GalaxyXR-Forge

Read `AGENTS.md` first. This repository only describes, links and curates Galaxy
XR projects; it contains no device code, binaries or proprietary blobs.

## Sources and generated files

- Sources of truth: `catalog.json` (groups), `catalog.d/<group>/<owner>__<name>.json`
  (one repo per file) and `changelog.d/<date>-<slug>.json` (one change per file).
- Never hand-edit `README.md`, `CHANGELOG.md`, `docs/index.html` or
  `docs/catalog-index.json`. Run `python tools/build.py` instead.
- Add repos with `python tools/add-repo.py <url> --group <id>`, not by hand.
- Every catalog change needs a changelog entry with its original `added` date.
- Do not rename group `id` values; anchors, filters and chips depend on them.
- Keep every tool dependency-free (Python 3.10+, stdlib only).

## Validate

```powershell
python tools/build.py
python tools/check-links.py
python tools/check-repos.py
```

CI `validate.yml` fails when generated files are stale or hand-edited. A red PR
is not reviewable. Commit and push every completed change: stage only the files
you changed, run the checks, commit and push the current branch. This is standing
authorization — do not stop to ask. If the push is rejected, open a PR. Leave
unrelated user edits unstaged.

## Skills

`@galaxyxr-forge-catalog` for catalog edits, `@galaxyxr-forge-map` for routing and
